WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:07.128
Aunt Polly was sitting alone in the dining room when Nancy brought in supper.

2
00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:12.222
"My niece will have to suffer the consequences for being late," Aunt Polly said.

3
00:00:12.223 --> 00:00:17.905
"When Pollyanna comes downstairs, she may have bread and milk in the kitchen."

4
00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:25.201
"Yes, ma'am." Nancy made a face, but fortunately Aunt Polly didn't catch her.

5
00:00:25.202 --> 00:00:29.825
Right after supper Nancy crept up the back stairs to the attic.

6
00:00:29.826 --> 00:00:35.098
"The poor lamb probably cried herself to sleep," Nancy said.

7
00:00:35.099 --> 00:00:37.703
She softly opened Pollyanna's door.

8
00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.764
The next moment she gave a frightened cry.

9
00:00:40.765 --> 00:00:45.775
"Pollyanna? Where are you?"

10
00:00:45.776 --> 00:00:50.652
Nancy looked in the closet, under the bed, and even in the trunk.

11
00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:55.125
Then she flew downstairs and out to the garden.

12
00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:58.743
"Tom! Pollyanna is missing!"

13
00:00:58.744 --> 00:01:06.138
"What?" Tom stopped tying some roses to a trellis.

14
00:01:06.139 --> 00:01:12.095
He scanned the horizon and pointed to a small figure silhouetted against the evening sky.

15
00:01:12.096 --> 00:01:15.705
"There she is—on top of that hill!"

16
00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:20.032
"Oh no! Miss Polly will see her!" Nancy said.

17
00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:27.797
"I don't want her to get a scolding. She's already in trouble for missing supper."

18
00:01:27.798 --> 00:01:32.877
By the time Nancy reached Pollyanna, the older girl was out of breath.

19
00:01:32.878 --> 00:01:39.304
"Pollyanna, you gave me a scare," Nancy said, panting.

20
00:01:39.305 --> 00:01:46.437
"I didn't know where you were!"

21
00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:52.901
"You don't need to worry about me," Pollyanna said as they came down the hill hand in hand.

22
00:01:52.902 --> 00:01:57.267
"Father and the Ladies' Aiders used to worry when I wandered off.

23
00:01:57.268 --> 00:02:01.261
Then they realized I always came back."

24
00:02:01.262 --> 00:02:06.587
"How did you leave your room without anyone seeing you?" Nancy asked.

25
00:02:06.588 --> 00:02:11.046
"I climbed down the tree outside my window."

26
00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:18.259
"Oh my goodness!" Nancy exclaimed. "I'd like to know what your aunt would say about that."

27
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:24.995
Pollyanna patted Nancy's arm. "Then I'll tell Aunt Polly, so you can find out!"

28
00:02:24.996 --> 00:02:31.570
Nancy's eyes widened in alarm. "No, no! Don't do that!"

29
00:02:31.571 --> 00:02:35.554
Pollyanna looked surprised but she nodded.

30
00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.661
"You must be hungry," Nancy said quickly.

31
00:02:38.662 --> 00:02:46.275
"But Miss Polly said you must eat bread and milk in the kitchen because you were late for supper."

32
00:02:46.276 --> 00:02:51.015
"I like bread and milk," Pollyanna said happily as they entered the kitchen.

33
00:02:51.016 --> 00:02:56.591
"And I won't have any trouble being glad about eating with you."

34
00:02:56.592 --> 00:03:01.805
Nancy remembered Pollyanna's brave attempt to like her attic room.

35
00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:06.464
"You don't have any trouble being glad about most things."

36
00:03:06.465 --> 00:03:12.324
Pollyanna laughed softly. "That's the whole point of the game."

37
00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:19.157
"The game?" Nancy gave Pollyanna a puzzled look as she set bread and milk on the table.

38
00:03:19.158 --> 00:03:25.849
"Yes, the Glad Game! Father and I played it all the time."

39
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.976
Pollyanna took a big drink of milk.

40
00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:32.237
"It all started when I wanted a doll.

41
00:03:32.238 --> 00:03:36.144
Every week Father looked in the donation box at church.

42
00:03:36.145 --> 00:03:42.715
There were all kinds of toys and clothes and other things in there, but no doll.

43
00:03:42.716 --> 00:03:47.844
Finally he brought home a pair of crutches that were just my size."

44
00:03:47.845 --> 00:03:51.224
"Crutches?" Nancy said.

45
00:03:51.225 --> 00:03:55.769
"Yes!" Pollyanna clapped her hands with glee.

46
00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:01.407
"It wasn't a doll, but Father said, 'Just be glad you don't need crutches!'

47
00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:06.235
And so we began playing a game to find things to be glad about.

48
00:04:06.236 --> 00:04:12.651
Sometimes it's difficult to think of something. But that makes the game even more fun!"

49
00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:16.410
Nancy was still skeptical.

50
00:04:16.411 --> 00:04:21.725
"It's going to be harder to play the game without Father," Pollyanna admitted.

51
00:04:21.726 --> 00:04:25.406
"But maybe Aunt Polly will play it with me."

52
00:04:25.407 --> 00:04:28.322
"I don't think so!" Nancy blurted out.

53
00:04:28.323 --> 00:04:33.084
Noticing the disappointment on Pollyanna's face, she quickly made a promise.

54
00:04:33.085 --> 00:04:37.732
"But I'll do my best to play it with you."

55
00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:42.677
That satisfied Pollyanna, who finished up her bread and milk.

56
00:04:42.678 --> 00:04:47.289
Then she went into the sitting room, where Aunt Polly was reading.

57
00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.946
"It's time for bed," Aunt Polly said.

58
00:04:50.947 --> 00:04:55.576
"I regret having to punish you on your first day here."

59
00:04:55.577 --> 00:04:58.329
"I was glad you did, Aunt Polly.

60
00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:05.586
I like bread and milk, and Nancy too. So don't feel bad about that."

61
00:05:05.587 --> 00:05:09.611
Pollyanna gave her aunt an affectionate hug.

62
00:05:09.612 --> 00:05:18.653
"I've had a wonderful time so far. I know I'm going to love living with you. Good night!"

63
00:05:18.654 --> 00:05:25.974
"What an unusual child!" Aunt Polly said to herself as Pollyanna ran from the room.

64
00:05:25.975 --> 00:05:30.490
But a few minutes later, Pollyanna was sobbing herself to sleep.

65
00:05:30.491 --> 00:05:34.925
"Oh, Father!" she said softly.

66
00:05:34.926 --> 00:05:45.481
"Even you would have trouble being glad about sleeping way up here by yourself."

